<Layout title="Privacy — Folklore"><article class="prose-page"><h1>Privacy</h1><p class="lede">Folklore v1.0.0 · November 23, 2026</p><h2>Search stays in your browser</h2><p>The website downloads a public catalog and searches it locally. Folklore does not send search descriptions to a model or a search server. Search and filter values are stored in the page URL so results can be shared. Hosting providers and anyone you share that URL with may see its query parameters.</p><h2>Local browser storage</h2><p>Saved entry IDs and your color-theme preference are stored in localStorage on this device. Folklore does not synchronize them across devices. Remove saved entries from their detail pages or clear this site’s browser data to remove that storage.</p><h2>Hosting and external links</h2><p>The site has no application analytics, advertising trackers, accounts, contact forms, or payments. The hosting provider receives ordinary network requests when you visit, including standard connection information. Folklore does not control provider infrastructure logs. Fonts and catalog files are served with the site.</p><p>Source links, GitHub, and external documentation operate under their own privacy policies. Following a link sends a request to that destination.</p><h2>Offline skill</h2><p>The downloaded skill and its lookup scripts read bundled local files. They contain no telemetry or network requests. Your coding agent’s provider and settings determine how it handles prompts and project context.</p><h2>Questions</h2><p>For questions about this implementation, <a href="https://github.com/Parthawe/folklore-ui/issues">open a GitHub issue</a>. Avoid posting private data in a public issue.</p></article></Layout>
